  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between (1R,4R,5R,9S)-4,5-epoxycaryophyllan-8(13)-ene and the CD276 antigen, as this compound is identified as a target of multiple entities that ultimately interact with CD276. Specifically, the compound is linked to HaCaT cells, which are known to express CD276, and multiple compounds that are targets of HaCaT cells, including 5,7,3',4',5'-Pentahydroxy-3,6,8-trimethoxyflavone, Ethyl 3-hydroxy-3-methylbutyrate, and (1R,4R)-4-Hydroxydauca-7-Ene-6,9-Dione. These compounds all have a shared target of CD276, indicating a possible pathway of action through HaCaT cells. The evidence suggests that the compound may act through a mechanism that involves targeting HaCaT cells, which in turn interact with CD276. The final score of 0.5002 across the three paths supports a plausible, though not fully conclusive, relationship between the compound and CD276. The mechanism appears to involve a cascade of interactions starting from the compound and ending at CD276, with HaCaT cells acting as a central node in this pathway.",
